# promise: #581
# A Little Window on a desktop stops being a non-activating panel once Cra comes forward with it. It opens as one, as
# Little Arc does, so it can come up over another app's full screen (#186), but the WindowServer never counts such a
# window as Cra's: picked in Mission Control or App Exposé with the browser window on another desktop, Cra came
# forward and the app the link came from took the front back as Mission Control closed. Cra comes forward as the pick
# lands, before Mission Control closes, so the window is an ordinary panel by then, AppKit's own flag included
# (prevents=, what the WindowServer goes by: the style alone changed nothing there). A background copy is refused real
# activation, so appActivated stands in for it.
budget rss=800 stalls50=20
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "defaultLinkDestination": {"littleWindow": {}}}
pace 0.5

cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=main
wait 2
cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=little
wait 3
cra://debug?littleActivation=opened
expect-log little activation opened: nonactivating=1 prevents=1 space=desktop

cra://debug?appActivated=1
wait 1
cra://debug?littleActivation=forward
expect-log little activation forward: nonactivating=0 prevents=0 space=desktop
